spans.s:
कल् कलयति (कलय˚ते) & कालयति pp. कलित
(q.v.) drive, impel;
 carry, bear;
 do, make, cause, produce, utter;
observe, notice;
 try, examine;
 suppose, think, regard as (2 acc.).
—आ shake, agitate, cast, fling;
 seize, tie, fasten;
 observe, notice;
try, etc. = S. उद् drive out, let loose. उप drive home. निन् drive
out, chase away. परि follow, pursue, seize, devour;
 consider or
regard as. प्र drive out, impel, pursue. सम् drive away, put to
flight;
 join, combine, be of opinion. — Cf. उत्कलित.

कल a. dumb, indistinct, low, soft (of sounds);
 n. adv. —
f. कला॑ q.v.

कला॑ f. a small part, esp. a sixteenth of the moon's orb;
 a
cert. small division of time;
 an art (there are 64).

1 काल f. ई dark-blue, black, m. the black part of the eye,
E. of Rudra-Śiva;
 N. of sev. kings etc., also = कालसर्प q.v.;
 f.
ई E. of Durga etc.

2 काल॑ m. time, esp. the right or proper time (w. gen., dat.,
loc., inf., or —˚);
 opportunity, case;
 season, mealtime (twice a day);
the half of a day, hour, age, era, measure of time, prosody;
 time as
ruler or destroyer of the world, i.e. destiny, fate;
 end;
 death or the
god of death. —परः कालः high time (w. inf.). कालं कृ appoint a
time for (loc.). कालेन in course of time (also ˚गच्छता;
 कालात् or
कालतस्), at times;
 कालेन दीर्घेण, बहुना, or महता (also gen.)
after a long time. कस्य चित्कालस्य after some time. काल˚ & काले॑
in time, at the right or appointed time;
 (also काले गच्छति) in
course of time, little by little. काले काले always in time or at the
right time. कस्मिंश्चित्काले one day. — उभौ कालौ morning and
evening. षष्ठे काले on the sixth half-day i.e. after three days;
पन्चशते काले after 250 days.

कलन a. causing, producing (—˚);
 f. आ driving,
impelling, performing, demeanour, gesture;
 n. shaking, agitating.

कलहंस m. a kind of duck, goose, or swan (f. ई);
 N.
of a man. — Abstr. ˚ता f.

कलाप m. band, bundle, quiver (also n.);
 a peacock's tail,
ornament i.g;
 totality.

1 कलि m. the One-side of a die;
 the last and worst of the 4
ages of the world;
 quarrel, strife (personified in all mgs).

2 कलि॑ m. a class of mythic beings;
 N. of a man, pl. his
race.

कलिका f. the sixteenth part of the moon's orb;
 a cert.
small division of time;
 an unblown flower. blossom.

कालिक a. relating to time;
 timely, season able;
 lasting as
long as (—˚).

कालिङ्ग a. coming from the country of the Kaliṅgas;
 m.
an inhabitant or king of it;
 f. ˚न्गी princess of the Kaliṅgas.

कलुष a. unclean, muddy, turbid (lit. & fig.);
 n. dirt,
stain, blemish.

क॑ल्पक a. normal, answering;
 stating, supposing (—˚);
m. ordinance, rule, precept.

कल्पन n. forming, imagining, cutting, fashioning;
 f. आ
the same + contrivance, arrangement, action, deed;
 form, shape.

कल्प्य a. to be made of (instr.);
 to be supposed, imagined,
or stated.

कल्मा॑ष f. ई black spotted. m. N. of a serpent demon;
f. कल्माषी a spotted cow;
 n. spot, stain.

कल्य a. well, healthy, ready, able, capable. n. health;
dawn, daybreak;
 an intoxicating drink. कल्यम्, कल्ये॑ & कल्य (˚—)
early.

कल्यवर्त (*m.) morning meal, breakfast;
 n. a trifle,
a little.

कल्या॑ण (f. कल्याणी॑) beautiful, lovely, good,
excellent, noble, auspicious, fortunate. f. ˚णी a kind of shrub;
 n.
fortune, happiness, virtue (p. ˚णिन्†);
 festival.

1 कालक a. dark-blue, black. m. mole, freckle, a sort of
grain. f. का॑लका a kind of bird;
 कालिका black spot, E. of Durgā.

कालकूट m. a poison produced at the churning of the
ocean;
 poison i.g.

कालक्षेप m. loss of time, delay;
 ˚क्षेपाय to win
time.

कालसूत्र n. the cord of the god of death;
 m. n. N. of a
certain hell.

कालिङ्ग˚क a. coming from the country of the Kaliṅgas;
m. an inhabitant or king of it;
 f. ˚न्गी princess of the Kaliṅgas.

कालीन a. relating to the time of —˚;
 also = कालिक
(—˚).

कालीयक m. N. of a serpent-demon;
 n. a kind of fragrant
black wood.
